## Synthesis of Ni-MOFs
In a typical optimized synthesis, $432\mathrm{\mg\Ni(NO_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6H_{2}O}$ , $150\mathrm{mg}$ trimesic acid and $1.5\mathrm{~g~}$ PVP, were dissolved in a $30~\mathrm{ml}$ mixture solution (distilled water:ethanol:D $\mathrm{{MF}}=1{:}1{:}1$ v/v/v) under vigorous stirring. The obtained light green solution was then transferred to a $50~\mathrm{ml}$ Teflon-lined autoclave and then heated to $150^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $10\mathrm{{h}}$ . The final products were centrifuged first at $4400\mathrm{rpm}$ for 10 min (Eppendorf $\textsuperscript{\textregistered}$ 5702) and washed with ethanol three times; the collected materials were dried in an oven overnight at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .
## Synthesis of NiO/Ni/Graphene Nanocomposite
The Ni-MOF powders were heated to $450^{\mathrm{{o}}}\mathrm{{C}}$ with a ramp-rate of $1\mathrm{{}^{\circ}C/m i n}$ and then held for $30\mathrm{min}$ . The whole annealing process was carried out in a tube furnace in Ar atmosphere. The resulting black powders were then heated to $200^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in air with a ramp-rate of $1\mathrm{{}^{o}C/m i n}$ and hold at $200^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for another $30\mathrm{min}$ to obtain the NiO/Ni/Graphene nanocomposite.
## Battery Fabrication
The electrode slurry was prepared by mixing $70\%$ active material, $15\%$ Super P and $15\%$ PAA ( $\mathrm{50~mg}$ in total) with NMP $(0.6~\mathrm{ml})$ ). The slurry was then cast on the copper foil and dried at $80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in an oven overnight. The coated copper electrode was punched into disks with a diameter of $7.98\mathrm{mm}$ by a hollow punch. The 2032 coin cells were assembled in an Argon filled glove box with oxygen and water content below 1 ppm. For the lithium ion battery, lithium foil is used as the counter electrode and the separator is Celgard (3501). The electrolyte is $1\mathbf{M}$ lithium hexafluorophosphate solution in EC and DEC $(1{:}1\ \mathrm{v/v})$ with $10\ \mathrm{wt\%}$ fluoroethylene carbonate.  For the sodium ion battery, sodium and glass fiber
## ACS Nano
membrane (Whatman, Cat. No. 1821 090) are used as counter electrode and separator, respectively. The electrolyte is $1\mathrm{~M~}$ sodium perchlorate in PC and EC $(1{:}1\ \mathrm{v/v})$ solution with $10\mathrm{wt\%}$ FEC.
